% The body of the test-duplabel documents: a display whose \label names a
% label an earlier display already used. LaTeX warns ("Label `x' multiply
% defined"), draws every display with its number, and a reference gives the
% last display's number and leads to it. Each case sits between "Before
% <case>." and "After <case>.", and its references follow in "Refs <case>:".
% The cases: two equations, an alignat with cases (twice), two rows of one
% align, three equations, a \qedhere display then an equation, an equation
% with its own \tag then a numbered one, two eqnarray rows, three \tag rows
% of one gather, a real label equal to a repeat with the next number
% appended, a real label repeated after a numbered repeat, multline and
% flalign, the starred displays with \tag (and \[ \] with \tag), and a
% display in a theorem. Then real labels named web-dup-1 and web-qed-2,
% which is the name the second \qedhere display's tag gets. Guards: a
% section's label used again by an equation, a label first on a \nonumber
% row, and one \tag row of a gather with a unique label. Then a repeat on a
% \qedhere equation, and on the \qedhere row of an align, a numbered display
% then a repeat with its own \tag, and, numbered by section, a real label
% equal to a repeat with the number appended. With cleveref,
% \cref leads to the last display too. (A reference to a \tag row is left
% out: its link has no target, with a unique label too.)
\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}
